This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} where $\beta>0$, $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, $0\ne f\in C(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{R})$, $0\ne F\in C^1(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{R})$ satisfy some conditions and note that the Ambrosetti-Berestycki type result in \cite{AB} is no longer applicable due to the biharmonic and Choquard type terms. By using a new homotopy lemma and a compactness lemma, we establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this type of equation. Moreover, we also prove the regularity of the solution. Finally, we provide an estimate for the norm of the solution. This type of equation arises in the study of stationary clouds of a type of dust grain in the Milky Way galaxy. This research was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program of Guizhou Provincial Education Department, the Science and Technology Research Program

